  data: {
    LLM: '1. **Ante and deal**: Players ante and receive initial cards. 2. **Betting round**: Poker-style pass/bet/call/raise/fold. 3. **Draw decision**: Surviving players may request one extra card or stand pat. 4. **Repeat**: Each draw cycle is followed by another betting round. 5. **Stop condition**: When no player takes another card, showdown occurs. 6. **Showdown split**: Nearest-to-7 winner takes half pot; nearest-to-27 winner takes half pot; ties split their half.',
    Player: '1. **Ante and deal**: Players ante and receive initial cards. 2. **Betting round**: Poker-style pass/bet/call/raise/fold. 3. **Draw decision**: Surviving players may request one extra card or stand pat. 4. **Repeat**: Each draw cycle is followed by another betting round. 5. **Stop condition**: When no player takes another card, showdown occurs. 6. **Showdown split**: Nearest-to-7 winner takes half pot; nearest-to-27 winner takes half pot; ties split their half.',
    objective: 'Win one or both pot halves by holding the total nearest to 7 and/or nearest to 27 at showdown.',
    gameplay: '1. **Ante and deal**: Players ante and receive initial cards. 2. **Betting round**: Poker-style pass/bet/call/raise/fold. 3. **Draw decision**: Surviving players may request one extra card or stand pat. 4. **Repeat**: Each draw cycle is followed by another betting round. 5. **Stop condition**: When no player takes another card, showdown occurs. 6. **Showdown split**: Nearest-to-7 winner takes half pot; nearest-to-27 winner takes half pot; ties split their half.',
    keyRules: [
      'Face cards are 0.5 each under standard rules.',
      'Aces are flexible (1 or 11) and can support both targets in evaluation.',
      'If all but one player folds, remaining player wins without showdown.',
      'House rule on above-target totals must be agreed before play.',
      'A perfect 5-A-A can evaluate to both 7 and 27 simultaneously.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
