    trumpBonusValues: null,
    setup: {
      players: '4-10 players in clockwise betting order.',
      deck: '52 cards. Number cards are face value; J/Q/K are 0.5 each; Ace counts as 1 or 11 (and can be interpreted differently for 7 and 27 in the same hand).',
      equipment: 'Cards and agreed betting stakes/limits.',
      dealing: 'Each player antes. Standard deal: one face-up and one face-down card to each player. Common variation: two face-down and one face-up initially.',
    },
    turnFlow: '1. **Ante and deal**: Players ante and receive initial cards. 2. **Betting round**: Poker-style pass/bet/call/raise/fold. 3. **Draw decision**: Surviving players may request one extra card or stand pat. 4. **Repeat**: Each draw cycle is followed by another betting round. 5. **Stop condition**: When no player takes another card, showdown occurs. 6. **Showdown split**: Nearest-to-7 winner takes half pot; nearest-to-27 winner takes half pot; ties split their half.',
