      'Setup example: 2 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Win one or both pot halves by holding the total nearest to 7 and/or nearest to 27 at showdown.',
      'Turn-flow example: 1. **Ante and deal**: Players ante and receive initial cards. 2. **Betting round**: Poker-style pass/bet/call/raise/fold. 3. **Draw decision**: Surviving players may request one extra card or stand pat. 4. **Repeat**: Each draw cycle is followed by another betting round. 5. **Stop condition**: When no player takes another card, showdown occurs. 6. **Showdown split**: Nearest-to-7 winner takes half pot; nearest-to-27 winner takes half pot; ties split their half.',
      'Scoring example: Split-pot payout between best 7-side and best 27-side totals among active players at showdown. Take the whole pot by winning both sides, or half pot by winning one target side..',
